{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>באברתו</b> — And the meaning is like (Deuteronomy 32:11), \"like an eagle stirring up its nest.\" And the meaning is that He will deliver him from the snare and from the pestilence. It is possible that \"the snare\" is the sword; therefore the word סוחרה (encircle him) is like צנה (buckler), as in: סחרו אל ארץ, Targum [reads it as] סביב (around). And so the meaning is: for the faithfulness of HaShem will surround him and enclose him."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 91, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:53.537318140Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}